		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: TYT MD-9600 V5 2571 Dead USB Port]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4175&amp;p=31829#p31829"><![CDATA[
I desoldered the antenna connections and pulled the PCB. Thermal paste is everywhere on the bottom of the board. I used a known-good USB cable and pulled the USB-A enclosure back enough to get my multimeter probe in and use the test points on the board. Unfortunately, the data pins both worked. So, the data makes it to the board, which means it's likely a failed surface mount component on the PCB.<br><br>I reassembled the radio and tested it. It still works fine for TX/RX on the channels it's programmed for.  Oh well. It's still a good radio. I'll learn how to program it manually. I may pick up a new one to experiment with OpenGD77 at some point.<br><br>Thanks again for all your help!<br><br>Jason / KC1UUF <br>73<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6338">KC1UUF</a> — Tue Jun 25, 2024 8:22 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
