This is the schematic and layout for the USB port. There are some test points which might help check the connection. <br><div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="http://localhost/opengd77/download/file.php?id=2466&amp;sid=94de1449851d68f8bbe06441bdec8eb6" class="postimage" alt="Screenshot_2024-06-25-09-50-48-489_com.google.android.apps.docs.jpg" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div><div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="http://localhost/opengd77/download/file.php?id=2467&amp;sid=94de1449851d68f8bbe06441bdec8eb6" class="postimage" alt="Screenshot_2024-06-25-10-09-32-118_com.google.android.apps.docs.jpg" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div>[]<br><br><br>USB_D- and USB_D+ connect directly to CPU pins 70 and 71. <br><br>Colin G4EML<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=87">G4EML</a> — Tue Jun 25, 2024 9:06 am</p><hr />
