		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4175&amp;p=31817#p31817"><![CDATA[
I can confirm that the TYT programming cable is just a standard USB cable. Any USB A to USB Mini cable should work. <br><br>You may need to check the soldering of the USB socket. That is the most likely failure point. <br><br>If you need to remove the PCB to do this it is fairly easy. Just remove lots of screws, unplug the fan and speaker and unsolder the short wire to the antenna connector.  The board should then lift out with the power cable attached. <br>Note that the screws are not all the same length, so make a note of where they come from. <br><br>Colin G4EML<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=87">G4EML</a> — Tue Jun 25, 2024 8:40 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
