		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4175&amp;p=31791#p31791"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>The official firmware USB device is not a com port<br><br>Try plugging the radio into a Linux box and list all the USB devices before and after connecting the radio</div></blockquote>Using my Mac:<br><div class="codebox"><p>CODE: </p><pre><code># Nothing plugged in% cat usb-nohub-1.txt +-o Root  &lt;class IORegistryEntry, id 0x100000100, retain 29&gt;  +-o AppleT8112USBXHCI@01000000  &lt;class AppleT8112USBXHCI, id 0x1000002e6, registered, matched, active, busy 0 (39 ms), retain 37&gt;  +-o AppleT8112USBXHCI@00000000  &lt;class AppleT8112USBXHCI, id 0x1000002cb, registered, matched, active, busy 0 (1719 ms), retain 218&gt;# Mac USB port to TYT-PROG-9600 cable to the MD-9600 USB port while the radio was on % cat usb-nohub-2.txt+-o Root  &lt;class IORegistryEntry, id 0x100000100, retain 29&gt;  +-o AppleT8112USBXHCI@01000000  &lt;class AppleT8112USBXHCI, id 0x1000002e6, registered, matched, active, busy 0 (39 ms), retain 37&gt;  +-o AppleT8112USBXHCI@00000000  &lt;class AppleT8112USBXHCI, id 0x1000002cb, registered, matched, active, busy 0 (1719 ms), retain 218&gt;# Removed the radio and cable and plugged in a USB flash drive% ioreg -p IOUSB &gt; usb-nohub-3.txt% cat usb-nohub-3.txt             +-o Root  &lt;class IORegistryEntry, id 0x100000100, retain 29&gt;  +-o AppleT8112USBXHCI@01000000  &lt;class AppleT8112USBXHCI, id 0x1000002e6, registered, matched, active, busy 0 (228 ms), retain 49&gt;  | +-o SanDisk 3.2 Gen1@01200000  &lt;class IOUSBHostDevice, id 0x10000d634, registered, matched, active, busy 0 (188 ms), retain 33&gt;  +-o AppleT8112USBXHCI@00000000  &lt;class AppleT8112USBXHCI, id 0x1000002cb, registered, matched, active, busy 0 (1719 ms), retain 218&gt;</code></pre></div>I think the USB port on the radio is damaged or disabled. I tested it with a normal USB-A to USB-B-mini cable and got the same results. Do you know of a way to disable the USB port? Have you ever heard of one failing but the radio continuing to work?<br><br>Thanks<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6338">KC1UUF</a> — Mon Jun 24, 2024 2:19 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
